---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import { SITE } from "../lib/blog-data.js";
import profilePicture from "../assets/Sumit_Lachung_profile_picture.jpg";
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`About - ${SITE.name}`}
  description="Sumit Datta's 16+ years of software engineering experience, entrepreneurial journey, core values, and work at startups across the US, Canada, Germany, and India."
  canonical="/about"
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-12">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: "Home", to: "/" }, { label: "About" }]} />

    <header class="mt-6 flex items-center gap-5">
      <Image
        src={profilePicture}
        alt="Sumit Datta"
        width={88}
        height={88}
        class="h-[88px] w-[88px] shrink-0 rounded-full object-cover"
      />
      <div>
        <div class="text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-primary">About</div>
        <h1 class="mt-1 font-serif text-4xl font-semibold leading-[1.05] sm:text-5xl">
          Sumit Datta
        </h1>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="prose-article mt-10">
      <p>
        I am Sumit Datta, an extremely passionate software engineer with 16 years of experience,
        mostly at fast-paced startups.
      </p>
      <p>
        I am entrepreneurial by nature, have built and failed at a few startups. I am very
        hands-on when it comes to software/product development. I am eager, curious and also a
        good listener. I have been part of, or built, or led teams in the US, Canada, Germany and
        India &mdash; although I have not been to the Americas.
      </p>
      <p>
        I blog about mental issues, personal journey, software and product development. This is
        my personal space and my views might seem contradictory to yours. That is OK, my views
        are not set in stone. This is a place where I share my learning as a human. Try not to
        take anything I share as advice &mdash; they are just my logs as I grow. If they help you,
        great! Share yours too and I will be happy to read. Cheers!
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
      <a
        href="/videos"
        class="inline-flex items-center rounded-md bg-primary px-5 py-2.5 text-sm font-medium text-primary-foreground hover:opacity-90"
      >
        My videos on vibe coding
      </a>
      <a
        href="/projects"
        class="inline-flex items-center rounded-md border border-border px-5 py-2.5 text-sm font-medium hover:bg-muted"
      >
        My software projects
      </a>
      <a
        href="https://calendly.com/sumitdatta/quick-chat"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        class="inline-flex items-center rounded-md border border-border px-5 py-2.5 text-sm font-medium hover:bg-muted"
      >
        Let's talk vibe coding (30m free!)
      </a>
    </div>

    <div class="prose-article mt-12 border-t border-border pt-10">
      <h2>My core values, guiding principles</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Build for the <strong>long term</strong></li>
        <li><strong>Motivated team</strong> is greater than the sum of individuals</li>
        <li><strong>Ownership</strong> &mdash; people do more when they are working for themselves</li>
        <li><strong>Refactor</strong> your product, <strong>iterate</strong> quickly &mdash; focus on user needs</li>
        <li>Build <strong>thin backends</strong> whenever possible, do more in frontend, close to the user</li>
        <li><strong>Processes</strong> are only as good as the people who practice them</li>
        <li><strong>Accept failure</strong>, every day you can start a new attempt</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Degrees and certificates</h2>
      <h3>Bachelor of Science in Computer Science</h3>
      <p>
        From <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/University_of_Calcutta" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">University of Calcutta</a> (2006).
      </p>
      <p>
        Successfully participated in <a href="https://summerofcode.withgoogle.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Summer of Code</a> 2006, for <a href="https://www.drupal.org/forum/general/news-and-announcements/2006-08-16/summer-of-code-2006-test-the-results" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Drupal</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Work experience</h2>

      <h3>Leader of Software Engineering at Hearth Display Inc.</h3>
      <p><em>November 2021 &ndash; October 2022</em></p>
      <p>
        I helped lay out the core software product with FastAPI, Python, PostgreSQL, React,
        Zustand, TypeScript and React Native. The Hearth application runs on a 27&rdquo; tablet
        (Android) with a React Native application and there are web applications with React. We
        built a RESTful API with FastAPI and Python, SQLAlchemy as ORM. I helped set up CI/CD
        with GitHub Actions, Ansible. I also helped mentor 2 younger engineers, worked with the
        Product Manager in setting up processes for regular work and hiring. I was working
        remotely from India.
      </p>

      <h3>Founder of dwata</h3>
      <p><em>November 2019 &ndash; September 2021</em></p>
      <p>
        I have been traveling around SE Asia for some headspace, and building <a href="https://dwata.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">dwata</a>, a data exploration tool that does not need any SQL knowledge. I joined On Deck (a platform for
        learning founders) in order to find like minded people and a potential co-founder. I also
        participated in Y Combinator Startup School in 2020. Since early 2021 I have been mainly
        collaborating on MVPs for other On Deck founders and experimenting on data exploration,
        no-code tools on the side.
      </p>

      <h3>Consultant &amp; Founder of Travlyng</h3>
      <p><em>August 2017 &ndash; November 2019</em></p>
      <p>
        Primarily worked as a consultant for a few startups (remotely from India). Moonlighted on
        my own product, <a href="https://twitter.com/travlyng" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Travlyng</a>, a network for avid travelers to sell their travel content as usable guides for
        other travelers.
      </p>

      <h3>Lead Developer at Mylittlejob GmbH</h3>
      <p><em>April 2015 &ndash; June 2017</em></p>
      <p>
        Worked with <a href="https://www.mylittlejob.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Mylittlejob GmbH</a>, leading a very small development team to build a Python (Falcon, SQLAlchemy), PostgreSQL,
        ReactJS (Redux, Router, FormatJS) based application. It is a marketplace for students to
        find online work &mdash; job creation, job management workflow, payment, payout, etc.
      </p>

      <h3>Python Developer at Smaato Inc.</h3>
      <p><em>September 2014 &ndash; March 2015</em></p>
      <p>
        Worked for <a href="https://www.smaato.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Smaato Inc</a>. In September 2014 I started working as a consultant Python developer for Smaato, working
        remotely from India. The project was built using Django, using MongoDB. In February 2015
        I joined the company as a full time employee in Hamburg, Germany. At Smaato I used
        Django, OAuth toolkit, DRF, Flask, Tornado for various projects &mdash; mostly building
        RESTful APIs.
      </p>

      <h3>Software Engineer at Eco Market</h3>
      <p><em>June 2013 &ndash; December 2013</em></p>
      <p>
        Worked with Eco Market (London, UK &mdash; remote) as Software Engineer. It is a
        marketplace for environmentally friendly, eco and natural products. Being part of a very
        small team, I looked into all aspects of development &mdash; most notably integration
        with Sailthru, user tracking and analytics, reporting with Chartio (SQL based), and
        implementing new designs handed over by a designer.
      </p>

      <h3>Software Engineer at Feastly</h3>
      <p><em>December 2012 &ndash; June 2013</em></p>
      <p>
        Worked with <a href="https://eatfeastly.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Feastly</a> (Washington DC &mdash; remote) as Software Engineer. It is a marketplace for cooks to host
        dinners at their convenient location. I was the sole engineer and looked into every
        aspect of the product development, from upgrading Django (1.3 to 1.5 with a custom user
        model), to new features, implementing new design, deployments, and payment processing
        (Balanced Payments/PayPal).
      </p>

      <h3>Senior Mentor</h3>
      <p><em>September 2012 &ndash; December 2012</em></p>
      <p>
        Consulted for a web development company as a senior mentor, looking over development,
        sales, technical support and internal processes. Introduced Yii (PHP), Git, Amazon Web
        Services, and memcached to the development team. Helped the sales teams consult
        prospective customers, understand needs and win projects.
      </p>

      <h3>Personal Sabbatical</h3>
      <p><em>January 2012 &ndash; August 2012</em></p>
      <p>
        Took a break from day jobs and tried working on some personal product concepts. Worked on
        an email/social based communication platform &mdash; planned as an inbox for Twitter,
        Email, Facebook, Feeds and other streaming content. Built with Node.js, Celery, RabbitMQ,
        MySQL, Python.
      </p>

      <h3>Framework Engineer at MobStac</h3>
      <p><em>July 2011 &ndash; December 2011</em></p>
      <p>
        Worked at <a href="https://www.beaconstac.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">MobStac</a> (Bangalore, India) as a Framework Engineer. This was the first company where I started
        working with Django. I worked on multiple aspects, from new features to bug fixing, a new
        Debian (.deb packaging) based deployment system, and an iPad-based simulated-native
        application in JavaScript (gesture recognition) for their TechCrunch Disrupt launch. The
        app had a native look and feel, powered by a custom built JavaScript rendering engine.
      </p>

      <h3>Tech Lead at forums.com</h3>
      <p><em>October 2009 &ndash; June 2011</em></p>
      <p>
        forums.com (Kolkata, India) tech lead. LAMP stack with Redis, Tokyo Cabinet, Gearman, some
        Python. I managed a team of 10, and looked into all aspects of operations and
        development.
      </p>

      <h3>Co-founder of Pixlie</h3>
      <p><em>December 2006 &ndash; December 2008</em></p>
      <p>
        Worked at Pixlie, a startup that I co-founded. Built hispanito.com as a social network on
        a LAMP stack, reaching 12 million page views/month with 100K+ monthly active users. Heavy
        memcached usage. Started working on Amazon Web Services.
      </p>

      <h3>Google Summer of Code</h3>
      <p><em>March 2006 &ndash; August 2006</em></p>
      <p>Google Summer of Code for Drupal, GData module development.</p>

      <h3>Project Lead at Intrasoft Technologies</h3>
      <p><em>2005 &ndash; December 2005</em></p>
      <p>
        Worked at Intrasoft Technologies <a href="http://www.123greetings.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">123greetings.com</a>, conceptualized and led their internal work/project management application
        &mdash; a task management tool for a 90-person company in an era when task management was
        still on pen and paper and the &ldquo;Intranet&rdquo; was still a word.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
